## Context

`config/corpus_collect.yaml` still sets `year_max: 2024`, so new API queries
cannot reliably add relevant 2025–2026 research. `config/analysis.yaml` also
ends the shared periodization at 2024. The REL decision is to harvest all
available research through the dated final search, include relevant 2025 and
2026 works (including working papers), present 2025 as the last complete year,
and flag 2026 as partial. The corpus pool is cumulative, so records already
dated 2025+ do not prove those years have been comprehensively searched.

## Actions

1. Specify and apply a Phase-1 collection window that reaches the final REL
   search date in 2026 across each relevant source, without silently admitting
   future-dated 2027 records as observations from 2026. Record the execution
   date and the actual publication-date rule used by each source.
2. Keep the REL analytic window separate from existing deliverables' pinned
   periodizations. Include 2025 in complete-year comparisons and report 2026
   separately as a partial year; working papers follow the same eligibility
   rule and are reconciled with later article versions.
3. Check every collector and downstream filter that reads
   `config/corpus_collect.yaml` or `config/analysis.yaml`; document what
   changes for REL and what remains pinned for other outputs.
4. Test inclusion of representative 2025 and pre-cutoff 2026 journal and
   working-paper records, exclusion or quarantine of future-dated records,
   and preservation of the existing outputs' configured windows.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A dated REL harvest covers 2025 and eligible 2026 works in available
      collection routes; the chosen cutoff is recorded with queries, and the
      unavailable Scopus route is disclosed by author decision.
- [x] 2025 and 2026 are distinguishable in the REL analytic data, with 2026
      marked partial; future-dated records receive an explicit disposition.
- [x] Other deliverables' periodization does not change unintentionally.
- [x] Changed-behaviour tests and the required corpus WP selection pass on padme,
      with the corpus available; the PR records the gate and resulting commit.

